<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lankatilaka Vihara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1344">1344</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lankatilaka is a Buddhist temple near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandy">Kandy</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, built in 1344 under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhuvanaikabahu-iv">Bhuvanaikabahu IV</a> of Gampola. Standing on a rock outcrop, its tall brick image house blends Sinhalese and south Indian styles and contains a large seated Buddha.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lankatilaka-vihara.jpg" alt="Lankatilaka Vihara" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BluesyPete · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lankathilaka_Vhihara_-_Le_temple.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
